Scroll containers: overflow Scroll and a host-driven scroll offset.

Upstream clips with `overflow-hidden` and leaves scrolling to JS, which moves
a child canvas with `translateY`. A host without a JS runtime has no way to
scroll a view. This adds the scroll container to the core and leaves the
input and the motion to the host:

- `Overflow::Scroll` (2): clipped like Hidden. Taffy lays it out as a scroll
  container, so its content keeps its size and runs past the box.
- Each node keeps a vertical scroll offset. Paint and hit testing place a
  scroll container's children moved up by it, so taps land on what is drawn.
  Readback records how far the content runs past the box, below it and, for
  `justify-end` content, above it (`Ui::scroll_bounds`), and clamps the
  offset to that.
- `Ui::scroll_target_at` finds the scroll container a drag at a point moves;
  `Ui::set_scroll` moves it, past either end while the host rubber-bands, and
  `Ui::set_scroll_bar` shows a scroll indicator along its right edge.

Applies after 0001-soft-wrap.patch. Nothing changes until a style uses
Overflow::Scroll, so upstream layouts and goldens do not change.

